To fix the issue of your app force closing when trying to set a wallpaper using an image loaded from the Picasso library, you will need to address the fact that network operations, including downloading images, cannot be done on the main thread. This leads to the `IllegalStateException` you're experiencing when your app tries to perform blocking calls like `Picasso.with(getApplicationContext()).load(...).get();`.

Instead of using the `get()` method, which is synchronous and can cause your application to freeze or crash, you should leverage the asynchronous nature of Picasso. Here’s how you can modify your code to properly load an image and set it as a wallpaper using a `Target`:

```java
class WallpaperTarget implements Target {
    private final WallpaperManager wallpaperManager;

    public WallpaperTarget(WallpaperManager wallpaperManager) {
        this.wallpaperManager = wallpaperManager;
    }

    @Override
    public void onBitmapLoaded(Bitmap bitmap, Picasso.LoadedFrom from) {
        try {
            wallpaperManager.setBitmap(bitmap);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void onBitmapFailed(Drawable errorDrawable) {
        // Handle the error here
    }

    @Override
    public void onPrepareLoad(Drawable placeHolderDrawable) {
        // Optional placeholder handling
    }
}

