<p>From my experiments, this is the thing that causes your problem.  In my code, when this is there <code>captureOutput:didOutputSampleBuffer:fromConnection</code> is not called.  I think the video system EITHER gives you a series of sample buffers OR records a compressed, optimised movie file to disk, not both.  (At least on iOS.)  I guess this makes sense/is not surprising but I have not seen it documented anywhere!</p>

<p>Also, at one point, I seemed to be getting errors and/or the buffer callback not occurring when I had the microphone on.  Again undocumented, these were error -11800 (unknown error).  But I cannot always reproduce that.</p>

